<<~ ahu slot=`#/ruling`>>

! Recipe Layer Model ~ a scout against the ruling

''Register: Model-Standing.'' A scout read the mount code, the routing cascade, the sync gate, the disk legs, the TW5 fork and the standing canon, whole; the operator ruled; two spirits enacted the model in the mounts, the cascade and the verbs. Every claim below names a file and a line; a claim without one names itself as inference. The #/as-mounted and #/as-routed sections describe the code AS IT STANDS; #/the-blur names what the enactment dissolved and what remains open.

''The operator's ruling, verbatim (quote license):''

> "For each recipe, the 'top bag' gets determined by the kind of raw tiddler. Most go to the 'named wiki bag' (disk projects into the base `/wikis/*` dir for the recipe), BUT `Draft of '...'` and similar tiddlers (#has `draft-of` field, etc) goes to a 'drafts' layer above that (fleet synced just as the wiki's main wiki-bag and the underlying canon-bags). Then there's volatile tiddlers on top of that (most don't sync, I think all here don't, Presence, local-only state, THIS is the per-device layer). Under the `wikis/` layers we have the 'canon bags' from `bags/` (disk ingest/projection-on-move). We need to deeply scout this blur and resolve the code and memes to one 'model architecture'. … Now that we have 'api surface' for memes and not just tiddlers this becomes important to clarify for all incoming files (other files would get ingested as typed tiddlers and round trip to disk with `*.meta` files, etc, so we may need to stub out or find the TW5 api surfaces for those non-tiddler/non-meme workflows)."

The ruling names FOUR strata per recipe — ''canon bags'' ← ''named wiki bag'' ← ''drafts'' ← ''volatile'' — and one routing key: ''the kind of raw tiddler''. The code mounts FIVE per-wiki slots plus a canon and a library floor — `personal` stands as its own layer by a later ruling — and routes drafts by the `draft.of` FIELD, volatile and view-state by kind.

''Five later rulings, verbatim (quote license):''

# Draft doc — "One doc -> fleet IF a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap available, ELSE this is a 'private device so far'. Pono? Our caps stack 'falls back to the floor' never fails/reds in production."
# `personal` — "Keep as its own layer, as we iterate on what 'needs fleet sync' vs what doesn't after the browser UX stands up."
# `meme get --recipe` — "The stack."
# The daemon wiki — "Approve `working` layers for all wikis (Daemon reads as a wiki with specific caps to the vessel, instead of 'user content')."
# The draft switch — "Approve moving to `draft.of` as the switch".

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/as-mounted`>>

!! The layers exactly as three composites mount them

Three `CompositeStore` instances stand in a running node, and one shape serves the browser. Bottom row first (lowest priority); the top row wins a read. ''`default`'' marks the layer the composite's UNBAGGED writes fall into — `addLayer` re-points `writableStore` at every layer registered with `writable:true` and `defaultWritable !== false` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/composite-store.ts:123`), so the LAST such layer holds the office. ONE law names that layer for every mounter: `slotLayerFlags` / `defaultWritableSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) — the working slot alone; no canon bag stands in, and the volatile temp slot NEVER holds the office. Witness: `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/composite-store.test.ts` "the default writable under the recipe layer model".

''Sync class'' reads off the node `sharePolicy`: every Automerge doc full-syncs to an in-process island peer and to a `same-operator` WS peer (the device fleet); a cross-operator peer reaches only the deterministically-federatable planes (`packages/lararium-node/src/self-slot-share.ts:70-95`, `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:434-462`). So ''fleet'' below means //any Automerge doc//; ''device'' means //a `MemoryTiddlerStore` that never enters a Repo//. The browser gate carries the same split (`packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts:370`, `:523`).

!!! A. The wiki ISLAND composite (node and browser — one kernel)

Laid by `expandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) walked bottom-up in `buildIslandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-recipe.ts`); slot docs resolve from typed grants in `sovereign-kernel.ts` `slotUrl`. The library bags a recipe RECORD names lay at boot (`recipeFromRecord`, read in `core-caps.ts` `mountCap` and `vessel-residency-wiring.ts` `resolveWikiSpec`), and recipe-watch keeps the same stack live.

| layer (top wins) | store | writable | default | sync class | doc keyed by | disk mirror (node) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/{slug}/temp` | `MemoryTiddlerStore` | yes | ''never'' (`slotLayerFlags`) | device | none — fresh per boot | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/draft` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet when seated · device when not | THE ONE slot-doc resolver (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`): `daemon/draft-bindings/{group}/{fingerprint}` (PersonaGroup × recipe-fingerprint, one row for each face) when the vessel holds a SEAT; else the floor doc `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{did}` in the catalog registry, `face-reach: vessel-only` | none |
| `wikis/{slug}/personal` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | the face's own devices | `daemon/personal-bindings/{group}/{fingerprint}` — one face's view-state and its PRIVATE MARGIN over the shared workbench (operator ruling 2026-11-11: //"Personal can absorb the new caps."//) | `<projections>/personal/<F>/{slug}/` via the `wikiSlot:"personal"` grant's `faceFolder` |
| `wikis/{slug}/working` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | ''YES'' — the ONE default | every member face | THE REALM WORKBENCH (cabal-realm#/the-workbench): the wiki's first stand under a face founds a private cabal of one and the vessel ledger notes it; the slot reads `realmWorkbenchDocUrl(realm, slug)`, and a share seats more faces without moving it. A vessel that wears no face stands none (`no-face`). The daemon wiki alone keeps its face-private device slot | `wikis/{slug}/`, or the workspace the wiki's share row names, via the `wikiSlot:"working"` grant (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `vessel-island-pool-core.ts`) |
| `bags/{slug}` (canon) | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | `grants.wikiUrl` = the catalog's `bags/{slug}` row; for a house-canon slug (`lares`, `lararium`, every disk-sourced holding but `crossroads`) the Kahu realm's standing document, which no catalog row names | `bags/{slug}/` via the `selfCanon` grant; `bags/lares/` and `bags/lararium/` by literal grants the Kahu's vessel alone holds |
| `libraryBags[]` | `AutomergeDocStore` | yes | no | fleet | the recipe record's `bag-stack` minus `structuralSlots` (the lares and lararium bags share library-layer behavior), laid at boot and reconciled live (`recipe-watch.ts`); recipe-watch resolves a library's document from the vessel's `@catalog`, and a house-canon library's from the Kahu realm's standing registration (`libraryDocUrl`), while genesis recipe seeds remain on `@oracle` | `bags/lares/` and `bags/lararium/` on the Kahu's vessel alone, `bags/crossroads/`, for the literal grants |
| `bags/oracle` (floor) | `floorReadFace` over an `AutomergeDocStore` | no | no | fleet · federatable | `grants.islandUrl`, beneath the pinned floor rows: one history-free snapshot per house-canon bag, resolved by the manifest CID the vessel pins (`floor-manifest.ts`) | none |

Two facts the table hides. (1) ''Every CRDT slot except the oracle floor registers `writable:true`'' — the floor mounts read-only, and a write aimed there copies up into the wiki's working layer. A working layer always mounts (operator ruling); `defaultWritableSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) names the working slot alone. (2) ''A hand's DELETE shadows a lower layer from working.'' `island-adaptor.ts` routes every hand tombstone through `_tombstoneBag`: a title that landed in the working layer or above it (a draft, a personal record) takes its tombstone where it lives; a title that landed beneath the working layer (a canon bag, writable or read-only) or from an unmounted bag takes an ordinary tombstone where its save would land (the layer the cascade names at or above the working layer: the temp slot for session state, the personal slot for a person's view state; else the working layer), and the lower bag receives no write. ''A hand's SAVE lands at or above the working layer, never beneath it'' (`_settle`, `_saveBag`): the cascade and its pointers choose among the layers the composition mounts there; a title that already lives in a layer above the cascade's choice stays where it lives, so the wiki shows the edit; a verdict naming a lower layer or an unmounted bag refuses by name on the alert rail and writes nothing (`wiki-shore-route.test.ts`). The composite resolves a title's topmost record, a tombstone included (`CompositeStore.resolveLayered`), and the wiki shows what that composition resolves. A wiki that mounts no working layer refuses the delete by name on the alert rail. Witnesses: `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/wiki-shore-shadow.test.ts`; `tests/lar-kind.test.ts` (a draft's delete lands in the draft slot). (3) ''At a veil floor the working layer rests in the vessel's own floor slot'' (`floor-slot/<slug>/working` in the control document, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/the-veil-ladder`>> #/the-base-model): the cascade reads the same, the document seals under the vessel's key, and the seat's landing moves its rows into the face's workbench.

!!! B. The daemon ISLAND composite (`recipe: { wikiSlug: "daemon" }`)

Same kernel (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-daemon-vm.ts`; browser `open-browser-vessel.ts`). The grants carry `islandUrl`, `wikiUrl` (= the daemon bag) and `catalogUrl` only, so at open `slotUrl` returns null for draft/working/personal; draft and personal slots prune for want of a handle, while `attachDaemonWorking` adds working afterward and `attachDaemonEditSlots` adds draft and personal after it, each a device slot of the face; `crossroads` splices in as a library (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts`). Then — the daemon reads as a wiki (ruling) — its own behavior LATE-ATTACHES a working layer: `attachDaemonWorking` (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts`) resolves `wikis/daemon/working` through THE ONE slot-doc resolver under the same binding law as every wiki, splices it above the daemon bag `defaultWritable: true`, registers the slot URI with keyhive (delegated to a seated face), and re-seeds `current-wiki-bag` to it. The attach runs after the keyhive and the veil stand, inside the fail-closed boot window; a failed attach refuses the boot by name (`WorkingLayerAttachRefusal`), and no canon bag stands in.

| layer (top wins) | writable | default | sync class | disk mirror |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/daemon/temp` | yes | never | device | `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>/temp/` only where the recipe designates it and the consent row names the slug (`daemonTempMirror`); else none |
| `wikis/daemon/working` (late-attached) | yes | ''YES'' | device: the daemon wiki's slots resolve as the face's device slots (`deviceScoped`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`; wired in `operator-daemon-behavior.ts`) | `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>/` (node, the worn face's folder) — `daemonWorkingMirror` (`packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts`) rides the daemon manifest's `diskMirrors` (`open-daemon-vm.ts`), mounted by `node-daemon-island.ts`'s `onBoot` → `mountDiskProjection` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/outbound-bridge`>>, `#/daemon-mirror`) |
| `bags/daemon-<F>` (the worn face's daemon canon, mounted while the face stands lit and proved) | yes | no | fleet (private plane) | `<projections>/bags/daemon-<F>/` — `daemonCanonMirror` |
| `bags/kahua` (the face's lift-only stage) | ''no'' — `slotLayerFlags` registers it read-only; only a signed lift or withdraw moves it | no | fleet (private plane) | `<projections>/bags/kahua-<F>/` — `kahuaStageMirror` |
| `bags/crossroads` | yes | no | fleet · federatable | the crossroads bag root by origin (`projectionRoots`: the canon source's `crossroads/` where it stands there, else `<projections>/bags/crossroads/`) (node) — the daemon designates it in its own mirror set (`open-daemon-vm.ts`), so a residency MOVE out of `wikis/daemon/working` publishes there |
| `bags/lares` · `bags/lararium` | yes | no | fleet | none here |
| `bags/daemon` (the daemon document: bindings; no control family rests here; beneath every library, `expandRecipe` in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) | yes | no | fleet (private plane) | none — no mirror names it |
| `bags/oracle` | no | no | fleet · federatable | none |

The two-vessel e2e witnesses the attach (`[daemon] working layer attached: lar:///ha.ka.ba/wikis/daemon/working`). A draft in the daemon wiki routes to `wikis/daemon/draft` — a bag with NO layer — and `composite.put` refuses loud; the daemon mounts `working` by ruling, never draft or personal. On a node the working layer projects to `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>/` (`open-daemon-vm.ts` `diskMirrors`, `daemonDiskMirrors` in `bag-paths.ts`); the daemon's receipts, ward audits and summons rest in the vessel control document (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/control-home.ts`), which no recipe composes and no mirror names, so the disk projector never meets them.

!!! C. The HOST composite (VM-free, one per vessel)

`assembleVessel` + `mountWikiSlot` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/open-vessel-core.ts`), invoked by `wikiCap` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts`) — which requires the daemon cap and awaits its `workerEa`, because the draft doc resolves through the daemon's slot-doc resolver (`resolveSlotDocs`, `vessel-steps.ts`) — the SAME call the island mount makes, so host and island mount ONE draft doc for one slug.

| layer (top wins) | writable | default | sync class | doc keyed by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wikis/{slug}/temp` | yes | never | device | fresh `MemoryTiddlerStore` |
| `wikis/{slug}/draft` | yes | no | fleet when seated · device when not | THE ONE slot-doc resolver, by the daemon proxy |
| `wikis/{slug}/working` | yes | ''yes'' — the host working layer | fleet | `wikis/{slug}/` |
| `bags/{slug}` | yes | no | fleet | catalog `bags/{slug}` |
| PersonaGroup · circles · identities · sessions · `bags/daemon` | yes | yes (no `defaultWritable` given → true; registered BELOW the wiki, so the wiki's canon shadows them) | fleet (private) | bootstrap |
| `bags/lares` · `bags/lararium` (live; mounted only where the Kahu realm names them, `keel.systemCanon`) | yes | no | fleet | the Kahu realm's standing registrations |
| `bags/oracle` | no | no | fleet · federatable | genesis |
| `bags/catalog` | ''no'' | — | fleet (private) | catalog-url file |

The host mounts the wiki's working layer as its default writable (`mountWikiSlot`, through `slotLayerFlags`) and mounts NO `personal` layer; the daemon's host composite takes `wikis/daemon/working` the same way (`mountHostWorkingLayer`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts`), after the worker answers its binding. A role cap composed alongside the core (the mesh palace, the WHO board) registers `writable:true, defaultWritable:false`: it takes a write that names its bag and never the working role, whatever order the caps compose in (`packages/lararium-mesh/tests/cap-layers-take-no-working-role.test.ts`). With no layer in the role a bagless write refuses by name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/as-routed`>>

!! The cascade ~ which KIND of tiddler lands where

The in-wiki cascade `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/config/bag-paths` (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/lar-bag-paths.tid:5-18`) walks newline-separated filters against the saving title; first non-empty result names the slot, an empty operand from a NAMED rule withholds, and no match names a router gap that still lands at `current-wiki-bag` with a console warning (`island-adaptor.ts` `_settle`). The cascade receives the title and its tiddler (`island-adaptor.ts` `_routeBag`): the pending-import, draft and personal-kind rules read tiddler fields, and every other rule reads the title alone.

| kind of raw tiddler | rule (`lar-bag-paths.tid`) | lands in | sync |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$:/core`, `$:/library/sjcl.js` | `:5-6` withhold | nowhere (engine bytes ride CAS) | — |
| `$:/temp/*`, `$:/status/*`, `$:/boot/*`, `$:/HistoryList*`, `$:/isEncrypted`, a pending import | `:7-12` | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | device |
| `$:/StoryList` and `$:/palette` (each by exact title), `$:/state/folded/*`, `$:/state/tab-*` — the set `lar-kind[]` names `personal` (`filters/lar-kind.ts`, ONE spelling; the cascade reads `[lar-kind[]match[personal]…]`) | `:13` | `wikis/{slug}/personal` | fleet |
| every other `$:/state/*` | `:14` | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | device |
| a tiddler whose `draft.of` FIELD stands (`[is[draft]…]`, TW5's own predicate) | `:15` | `wikis/{slug}/draft` | fleet |
| `lar:*` | `:16` | `current-wiki-bag` = `wikis/{slug}/working`, the daemon wiki included | fleet |
| anything else, including a foreign-titled pack member (`HelloThere`) and every other `$:/` system tiddler | `:17` catch-all | `current-wiki-bag` | fleet |

''The `draft.of` FIELD is the switch'' (operator ruling 2026-09-11, quote license: "Approve moving to `draft.of` as the switch (pono w/ TW5 server/client setups)"). TW5 decides draft-ness by that field (`TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/tiddler.js:20-22`) and mints the title through a LOCALIZED language string — `Draft/Title`, or `Draft/Attribution` when `$:/status/UserName` stands, yielding `Draft of 'X' by <user>` (`TiddlyWiki5/core/modules/wiki.js:1725-1735`) — so the title decides nothing: the cascade's draft rule reads `[is[draft]…]` and `lar-kind[]` reads `Tiddler.isDraft`, on a stock server and an island alike (`tests/lar-kind.test.ts`; the live-server witness in `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts`). The ruling's spelling `draft-of` (hyphen) names no TW5 field; TW5 spells it `draft.of`. ''The delete path:'' a delete runs after the tiddler has gone, so the field cannot be read then. `_flushHand` takes the bag of this shore's last acknowledged write of the title first, then the landed ledger's bag; for a title neither knows, it falls back to the cascade's title read. `_tombstoneBag` places the tombstone by layer order: a still-recorded title from working or above takes that layer, while a title from beneath working takes the cascade's eligible layer or working. A draft's own deletion in a save, rename or cancel starts from the draft book's bag (`_actBody`); `_tombstoneBag` chooses the layer, and `_handBaseFor` supplies that title's hand or landed base. Witness: `tests/lar-kind.test.ts` "deleting a draft tombstones in the DRAFT slot, not working".

''What the nalu stamps.'' `toWikiFields` stamps `$origin-bag` from the envelope, and `_landOne` stamps it on shore landing (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/nalu-engine.ts`; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts`). The projector routes a flush by that stamp (`packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts` `flush`), and `_buildFamily` strips it before the put (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts`). No field on a saved tiddler names its destination bag: `draft.of` selects the draft route, and a draft's store-only base fields record its target's base and route nothing.

!!! Verb seats

| seat | resolves the bag how | lands in | file:line |
|---|---|---|---|
| in-wiki edit / save | the cascade, by kind — `IslandAdaptor.saveTiddler` | per the table above | `island-adaptor.ts` `saveTiddler` / `_writeMeme` — MEASURED: `outbound-bridge.ts`'s `change` listener (wired by `sovereign-kernel.ts` through `bridgeWikiToAdaptor`) reads each wiki change dispatch once the shore turns resident and calls `saveTiddler` or `deleteTiddler`; `$tw.syncer` does not run. The seat holds and the wire stands |
| in-wiki delete | the bag the title landed from → `_tombstoneBag` | that bag while its layer stands at or above working and holds a record for the title; otherwise the layer the cascade names at or above working, else the working layer | `island-adaptor.ts` `_tombstoneBag` |
| `meme put --recipe default` | the daemon's own wiki anchor | its daemon working layer | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts` `readContainer` and `anchorBagOf` |
| `meme put --recipe <slug>` | THE PUT LAW: the recipe RECORD's `writable-bag` = `wikis/<slug>/working`, else the top of its `bag-stack` (`designatedBagOf`, `@lararium/mesh` recipe.ts) → a mounted writable layer of the DAEMON island, else the instance slot's doc through THE ONE slot-doc resolver, else reach by catalog | the SAME working doc the wiki island mounts — the placement surfaces in the running wiki (two-vessel e2e ⑤ ★) | `meme-verbs.ts` `reachRecipeBag` / `storeOfBag` |
| `meme get --recipe <slug>` | THE GET LAW: the whole cascade top-down (`expandRecipe(recipeFromRecord(rec))`), the first bag holding a RECORD under the root, live or tombstoned, as the wiki's own composite reads it; the designated bag's store when none does (a null read, never a refusal) | the stack — draft shadows canon; canon answers through `--recipe` when the drafts hold nothing; a tombstone in a bag above shadows canon, so a carrier the wiki removed reads `not-found` | `meme-verbs.ts` `reachRecipeBag`; `tests/meme-verbs.test.ts` "READS THE STACK" |
| `meme list --recipe <slug>` | THE LIST LAW: the same cascade the get walks; every root some bag of the stack holds, each answered by the first bag that holds a record under it, so a tombstone above shadows the bags beneath and a root two bags hold lists once | the stack — each row names the bag that answered; a bag the island neither mounts nor reaches gets named `unreached`; `meme list --bag` lists that one bag's own records. Every listing pages at the outcome's row cap (`MEME_LIST_PAGE`) and names the cursor of the next page | `meme-verbs.ts` `listRecipeStack`; `tests/meme-verbs.test.ts` "a named recipe lists the roots its stack resolves" |
| `meme put --bag <slug>` | `compositeMemeSink` → `composite.put({bag})` on the daemon island | that bag's writable layer, else refuses (no shadow-up) | `meme-verbs.ts:177-179`, `composite-store.ts:218-244` |
| `act ADD / COPY / MOVE / LOAD / INGEST --to <bag>` | `BagAccess`: a mounted writable layer, else the catalog/oracle accessor's own store (write-then-sync) | the named bag exactly | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/action-handler.ts:243-270`, `:1170-1186` |
| `lares ingest --source <dir> --to <bag>` | the caller names `--to`; a `wikis/` source only changes the URI derivation | the named bag | `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/ingest.ts:27-33`, `packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts:118-131` |
| `draft` verb (`makeDraftReactor`) | `toBag` else `defaultWritableBagId()` | the daemon's working layer by default | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-draft-handlers.ts` |
| `where` / `wiki which` | the mounted composite, every registered bag by access, AND every registered wiki's instance slots through THE ONE resolver (a floor doc answers under its slot name, never its registry key) | membership | `packages/lararium-tw5/src/worker-data-verbs.ts` `makeWhereReactor` |
| recipe-watch library mount | `bag-stack` minus `structuralSlots(slug)` | inserted above `bags/lares`, `writable:true, defaultWritable:false` | `recipe-watch.ts` |

''The recipe record and the mount struct spell ONE shape.'' `recipeRecordFields(recipe)` (`@lararium/mesh` wiki-recipe.ts) writes `bag-stack` = the expanded cascade bottom-up minus the four instance slots (the oracle floor, the libraries, the wiki's own canon) and `writable-bag` = `wikis/{slug}/working`; `recipeFromRecord(rec, slug)` reads it back; both minters call it (`genesis-doc.ts` `systemRecipe`; `wiki-mint-handlers.ts` init). The catalog registry never rides a bag-stack (access ≠ load). `CompositeStore.getRecipe` / `putViaRecipe` / `buildLayersFromRecipe` and the camelCase `RecipeTiddler` are retired. Witness: `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/recipe-record.test.ts`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/as-written`>>

!! What the canon carriers say, and where they contradict the code or each other

| carrier | says | the code | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| `wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law` (`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology.mem:181`) | "a draft/volatile tiddler → `@temp`" | `Draft of ` routes to the CRDT `draft` slot (`lar-bag-paths.tid:16`) | contradicted the code AND the ruling — HEALED by the aftermath spiral (the law now reads `@draft` for drafts, `@temp` for volatile) |
