<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-blur`>>

!! The blur, named

# ''`writable-bag` vs the mount's default'' — DISSOLVED. The record designates `wikis/{slug}/working`; `defaultWritableSlot` names that slot, and the mounted working layer receives default writes.
# ''Two draft documents wear one slot name'' — DISSOLVED. THE ONE slot-doc resolver (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/slot-doc-resolver.ts`, the law `resolveSlotDoc` in `@lararium/mesh`): the PersonaGroup × fingerprint binding WHEN the vessel holds a seated PersonaGroup cap, ELSE the device floor `wikis/{slug}/drafts/{did}` — and the record says which (`face-reach`). Every site reads through it: the island's slot grants, the host mount (by the daemon proxy), `wiki init`, `prune-stale`, `meme put --recipe`, `where`, the ACTION verbs. Weld witness: `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/slot-doc-resolver.test.ts` S3 (five sites, one doc, seated and unseated). ⚠ THE MOUNT'S TRACE IS THE TRACE: a wiki the vessel mounted this session fingerprinted the canon doc it holds; a verb re-deriving the url from a registry pointer read a DIFFERENT doc when a peer's founding rewrote the shared oracle plane's `bags/lares` pointer mid-session (measured in the two-vessel e2e) — the resolver keeps the mount's trace per slug and reuses it.
# ''Per-DID or per-PersonaGroup'' — RULED: both, by seat. Fleet when a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands; the DID floor when not — a private device so far. A seat landing later resolves the face doc from then on; the floor stays the device's own (no migration).
# ''What "volatile / per-device" holds: temp ALONE.'' Presence stands unbuilt — no `presence` slot, no `$:/status/` beyond what TW5 writes; `$:/status/*` and `$:/boot/*` and most `$:/state/*` route to temp (`lar-bag-paths.tid:8-10`, `:15`). `personal` syncs across the face's own devices by design (its view state and private margin), so the ruling's "all here don't [sync]" holds for temp and not for personal. Per-device state that MUST survive a reboot (a device's own window layout, a local-only bag pin) has no home: temp forgets at boot, personal follows the face's devices.
# ''A draft routes by its `draft.of` FIELD on SAVE; DELETE placement follows the landed ledger and layer order.'' RULED (the field drives the switch). The cascade's `[is[draft]…]` reads the tiddler the save carries; `_flushHand` takes the bag of this shore's last acknowledged write of the title first, then the landed ledger's bag, and falls back to the cascade's title read when neither knows the title. `_tombstoneBag` chooses the eligible layer by composition order; a draft's own deletion in a save, rename or cancel starts from its draft-book bag (`_actBody`), and `_tombstoneBag` chooses the layer. Witness: `tests/lar-kind.test.ts`.
# ''A non-meme file enters by three doors and leaves by one, and foreign titles leave by none.'' Enter: (a) `lares ingest --source --to` scans `.mem` and any extension, pairs a `.meta` sidecar, derives the URI by the address siting rule (`ingest-core.ts:83-88`, `:111-113`, `:171-181`); the island runs `tw5.parseFields(meta)` then `tw5.deserialize(ext, text, base)` (`action-handler.ts:863-873`) and packs foreign-titled members into `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (`:815-833`). (b) `act LOAD --to` takes carriers with the verb, same registry route (`:641-707`). (c) the in-wiki drag-drop / `$:/Import` ride TW5's own DOM deserializer and then the cascade — no house code touches it. Leave: the ONE render shore `exportCarrierFile` (`meme-write.ts:40-77`) → `makeTw5FileInfo` (`tw5-file-info.ts:88-176`) picks `.tid` / content + `.meta` / `.json` exactly as `generateTiddlerFileInfo` does, base64 for a binary type (`:140`), and the projector sites it at `<uri-path><ext>` (`disk-projector.ts` `flush`). But `carrierBaseRelPath` sites only `lar:///w.w.w/…` names (`bag-paths.ts:84-99`): a `.png` ingested under a `lar:` URI round-trips; a `HelloThere.tid` pack member reaches disk only through REPACK of its pack (`action-handler.ts:352-370`).
# ''`meme get --recipe` reads the designated bag, not the stack'' — DISSOLVED by ruling ("The stack."). GET walks the whole cascade top-down and answers from the first bag holding a record under the root, where a tombstone answers the meme absent; PUT writes the designated bag alone. Witness: `tests/meme-verbs.test.ts` "READS THE STACK"; two-vessel e2e ⑦ ★ (canon answers through `--recipe` on B).
# ''Two recipe shapes, one name'' — DISSOLVED. `recipeRecordFields` ⇆ `recipeFromRecord` (`@lararium/mesh` wiki-recipe.ts); `catalog` leaves the user stack; the live lares bag mounts as a library like the lararium bag (a record that names it mounts it), and the system recipes alone name either: every other wiki reads both through the floor's snapshots. The libraries a record names lay at boot AND reconcile live.
# ''`working` and `personal` against the four strata'' — RULED. "named wiki bag" = `working`; `personal` keeps its own layer. The daemon wiki also mounts a working layer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/one-model`>>

!! One model ~ the fewest changes that satisfy the ruling

''The layer list per recipe'' (bottom → top), reading the ruling's four strata onto the slots that already exist:

| ruling stratum | slot | store | sync | disk | writable | default |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| canon bags | `bags/oracle` · `libraryBags[]` · `bags/{slug}` | CRDT | fleet (+ federatable where the plane allows) | `bags/{name}/` on ingest and on promotion MOVE | by ACTION verb only | no |
| named wiki bag | `wikis/{slug}/working` | CRDT | fleet | `wikis/{slug}/` | the cascade's catch-all | ''YES — the ONE default'' |
| drafts | `wikis/{slug}/draft` (absorbs `personal` as a KIND, see below) | CRDT | fleet | none | the cascade's draft rule | no |
| volatile | `wikis/{slug}/temp` | memory | device | none | the cascade's temp rules | no |

''What stands'' (each red-first, each witnessed): the working slot holds the default writable office (mesh `slotLayerFlags`; witnesses in `composite-store.test.ts`); a hand's delete of a title beneath the working layer tombstones in working, or in the upper layer the cascade names for that title (`wiki-shore-shadow.test.ts`, `wiki-shore-route.test.ts`); ONE slot-doc resolver, floor-falling (`slot-doc-resolver.test.ts`); `meme get --recipe` reads the stack, `meme put --recipe` writes the designated bag (`meme-verbs.test.ts`); the recipe record and the mount struct converge (`recipe-record.test.ts`); the daemon attaches its `working` layer or refuses the boot (two-vessel e2e); `wiki init` registers `wikis/{slug}/working` and the vessel's `registerBags` carries it, so the cap gate knows the working slot; the `.meta` sidecar merges OVER the deserialized record as TW5's loader rules (`action-handler.ts`, both doors).

''What remains'' (owed, named):

* ''A stale catalog row for house canon.'' No mount files a row for a house-canon bag: a wiki standing on one mounts the Kahu realm's standing document where the vessel holds it, and where it holds none `mountWikiSlot` mints no document, lays no canon layer, and keys the slot bindings on the bag's floor address (`floorCanonAddress`). One resolver (`resolveHouseCanon`) answers every door, the realm's standing document first (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/offering`>> #/the-canon-offer). A vessel that booted under the earlier mount may still hold a `bags/lares` row in its catalog; it answers no door where the realm names a document, and it still answers where the realm names none. Burning that row stays owed.
* ''Disk legs for non-meme files:'' the siting cascades ride (#/tw5-surfaces); binaries under `bags/` read OPEN (talk-story).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/questions`>>

!! Questions the operator answered, and the one still open

# ''Does a draft fleet-sync, or stay on the device?'' RULED: fleet when a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands, else the device floor; the cap-stack falls to the floor, never reds.
# ''Does `personal` survive as a layer?'' RULED: its own layer, while the browser UX stands up.
# ''Which per-device state MUST survive a reboot?'' OPEN. Temp forgets; personal follows the fleet; the draft floor of an unseated vessel stands as the one per-device CRDT doc.
# ''Does "named wiki bag" mean `working`?'' RULED by the disk sentence: `working`; the shore-law MOVE stays the promotion door.
# ''Does `meme get --recipe` read the stack?'' RULED: "The stack."
# ''Does the `draft.of` FIELD decide routing?'' RULED: `draft.of` drives draft routing; DELETE placement follows the landed ledger and layer order.
# ''Which non-meme file types enter through `lares ingest`?'' Every extension, through TW5's registry; binaries under `bags/` read OPEN (talk-story).
# ''Does the daemon wiki gain its `working` layer?'' RULED: working layers for all wikis; the late attach stands.
# ''Do the route skins and the in-VM face ship as one bundle, or two?'' RULED: ''one bundle, the caps decide what rings''. The ruling, its three grounds and what it leaves open stand at #/one-bundle.

<<~/ahu>>

