''Reading.'' The house stands on the registry and the deserializer chain, re-implements the filesystem module's pure half (parity-witnessed against the fork's own module), reads the siting cascades as the adaptor reads them, and answers the kind of a raw tiddler by TW5's own predicates. What it lacks names itself: the disk walker's `tiddlywiki.files` and plugin-folder legs (never needed while `ingest` reads declarations).

''The non-meme round trip, measured'' (`tests/e2e/nonmeme-parity.test.ts`, both doors real): `note.md` + `.meta` — bytes identical, fields identical; `pack.json` — both doors keep the membership in `$:/config/OriginalTiddlerPaths` (the server only under `retain-original-tiddler-path`), and the server's `--savewikifolder` explodes the pack into per-member `.tid` files where the island keeps it packed (REPACK) — named, on purpose. Two strays: (1) the island seeds the `.meta` BEFORE the deserialize (`action-handler.ts:870-873`) where TW5 merges it AFTER (`boot.js:1961`), so `type: text/markdown` in a sidecar lands as `text/x-markdown` on the island — a red held in the witness, owed to `action-handler.ts`; (2) `$origin-bag` reached the sidecar — cured in `tw5-file-info.ts` (`UNPERSISTED_FIELDS`). MEASURED, OPEN: a `.png` under bags/ enters the island as a skinny handle `photo.tid` on the `cid/` tier and the `.png` sweeps; the server keeps `photo.png` + `.meta` whole.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/one-bundle`>>

!! One bundle ~ the caps decide what rings (operator ruling, 2026-09-11)

''The ruling, verbatim (quote license).'' The operator read the eight Basket-One loops and ruled on all of them; the eighth clause reads:

> "one bundle, the caps decide what rings (operator)"

''What it settles.'' The meme verbs stand as //"the daemon island's skins of the meme laws"//, and //"every skin (this, the HTTP route, the MCP tool) carries verbatim"// one contract, with //"the anchor project[ing] through the in-VM face (`$tw.lares.meme.project`)"// (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts:2-11`). The question stood: do the route skins and the in-VM face ship as ONE bundle, or split by tier. ''They ship as one.'' The route skins, the in-VM face and the engine ride a single plugin, and a vessel's declared cap-stack decides which of them rings on that vessel.

''The three grounds the ruling rests on.''

# ''One law shipped twice reads as two laws.'' The contract every skin carries VERBATIM already reads as ONE law. A split bundle carries it in two artifacts that must be tuned together, and the hand-derived enumeration drifts the way every hand-derived enumeration drifts. One casting rings the same law at the road, the gate and the sanctum; two castings drift by a hair a year and nobody notices until a reader does.
# ''The keel already answers it, for free.'' <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/composable-keel`>> `#/absence-is-structural` rules that a Herm reads as //a cap-stack that never declares the wiki cap// and runs //blind by structure, never by a flag a later bug could flip// — //an absent cap grants no authority//. ''One keel, two `#has`-stacks: the same code, thinned by caps, never two codes.'' A bundle split by tier re-spells that thinning in packaging, where the composition root already spells it in wiring — and packaging cannot fail closed. This carrier's own cap posture reads the same direction at #/questions: //the cap-stack falls to the floor, never reds//.
# ''What travels stays a cap question, never a bundle question.'' Whether the road-bells — the HTTP route, the MCP tool — ring on a given vessel answers off that vessel's declared stack. A wayfarer that declares no sanctum rings no sanctum-bell, and it does so without a second artifact existing.

''Where the bundle stands, measured.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json` ships as ONE plugin tiddler carrying `nalu-engine` and `bag-paths` and no syncadaptor (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/outbound-bridge`>>, `#/island-holds`). Road A of the bridge would have added a packed module to that same bundle, applying //the same law to the daemon island and the wiki island alike (one plugin)// (`outbound-bridge.mem` `#/back-parity`) — the ruling holds either road, because it rules the artifact count rather than the wire.

''Where the ruling was told.'' The stories that set the intent ride at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/scale-stories-basket-one`>> `#/one-plugin-or-two`, and the moʻolelo carrying all eight clauses rides at that floor's `#/exit`. ''That floor holds the telling; this carrier holds the ruling.''

⚠ ''What the ruling does NOT settle.'' It fixes the artifact count at one. It says nothing about which caps gate which skin, nor about the manifest shape a thinned bundle presents to a vessel that declares less than the whole. Those stand open here.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/aftermath`>>

!! Aftermath ~ the blast-radius spiral (operator-approved)

The spiral walked every carrier the #/as-written table names and evergreened the ones whose text described retired code: `wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law` (drafts → `@draft`, volatile → `@temp`, title-read), `save-path` SP-3/SP-4 (the cascade rule; the envelope law, no `bag` field routes), `disk-projection#/projection-routing` (the siting requirement for rule 2; rule 3 marked OWED), `residency-model#/yang-yin-chao` (temp outside the keyed set), `bag-wiki-uri-split` meta (`standing`, half-enactment named). The `lares-history` tree stays untouched (history, never canon).

''Tensions the first spiral surfaced, and how they closed:'' `wiki-layer-ontology#/naming-law` — re-trued to carve the draft FLOOR out (a per-DID device doc, a registry entry, never an instance mount of a group); `personal-slot#/scoping-mechanism` — the seat decides (binding when seated, floor when not); the four strata against five slots — ruled (`working` is the named wiki bag, `personal` stays); the `draft.of` field — ruled (the switch, with the delete map); the default writable = temp — cured red-first. What remains stands under #/one-model "What remains".

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/daemon-and-domain`>>

!! Daemon wiki and domain wiki ~ two recipes, side by side

''The operator's ask, verbatim (quote license, 2026-11-14):''

> "since we use the recipe/bags model and not a single invariant-store for each Wiki (I mean, that exist above the CRDT bags 'recipe') then we have to use the `kapae` shadow-tombstone pattern sometimes when 'deleting' (imagine a recipe with the same tiddler in 3 bags, but the user decided to 'Delete' the top -> ??? vs 'kapae(shadows the underneath as also-deleted)/delete(reveals the underneath)'. Do we have a meme or ahu that clearly describes the 'recipe' differences between Daemon Wikis and Domain Wikis? Find a pono place, and write that."

''Register: Model-Standing, measured 2026-11-14.'' Before this slot no one carrier set the two recipes side by side: #/as-mounted lays the island, daemon and host composites by MOUNT, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm`>> #/the-workbench rules the carry law by CAP CONTRACT, and <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage`>> #/the-recipe tells the daemon stack by ORGAN. This slot reads all three against the code, a row per layer, top row winning a read.

''Two classes, one kernel.'' A ''daemon wiki'' (`recipe: "default"`, slug `daemon`) holds ONE face's memory on ONE device: every slot it writes stays face-private, so it seeds, exports and imports per face (operator, 2026-11-14: //"daemon wikis should seed per-face"//). A ''domain wiki'' (a house wiki: `lares`, `lararium`, `elyncia`, `sdm`, `crossroads`; or one `wiki init` mints, such as `notes`) holds a shared working layer, the realm workbench, which every face its contract seats reads and writes: one document, one folder, one seed (//"most wikis should NOT seed per-face because shared crdts"//). The ''veil floor'' (a vessel wearing no face) stands either class in its own vessel-keyed documents. One `expandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) orders every stack: temp, draft, personal, working, the wiki's canon, the libraries, the wiki's own bag where its canon follows a face, the oracle floor.

| layer (top wins) | daemon wiki (face `F` worn) | domain wiki (`<slug>`) | veil floor (no face) |
|---|---|---|---|
| ''temp'' | `wikis/daemon/temp`: a fresh `MemoryTiddlerStore` each boot; the device alone; mirrors to `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>/temp/` only under a consent row (`daemonTempMirror`) | `wikis/<slug>/temp`: the same store and life; no mirror unless a consent row names the slug | the same; nothing seals it, nothing carries it |
| ''draft'' | `wikis/daemon/draft`: absent at open (no slot handle, #/as-mounted B), then late-attached as a face's DEVICE slot beside working (`attachDaemonEditSlots`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts:554-581`; `deviceSlot`, `slot-doc-resolver.ts`); mounted writable, never the default write layer; takes the engine's `Draft of …` records by the recipe's own routing; a floor whose rest key does not stand holds it in the island's memory alone | `wikis/<slug>/draft`: a seated face's binding (PersonaGroup × fingerprint), else the vessel's floor doc `wikis/<slug>/drafts/<did>`; no disk mirror (its `recovery/` holds one face's hand) | the DID floor doc, `face-reach: vessel-only` |
| ''personal'' | `wikis/daemon/personal`: absent at open, then late-attached as a face's DEVICE slot the same way; mounted writable, never the default write layer; takes the engine's story list and view-state; face-private on one device, as every daemon slot | `wikis/<slug>/personal`: ONE face's view-state and private margin; crosses that face's own devices; projects to `<projections>/personal/<F>/<slug>/`; seeds, exports and imports per face; the default write layer for a face that holds no writer's seat in the workbench (`slotLayerFlags` with `writeSlot: "personal"`) | the vessel's floor slot for `personal` (`floorSlot`, `slot-doc-resolver.ts`) |
| ''working'' (the default write layer) | `wikis/daemon/working`: the face's DEVICE slot (`deviceScoped`), late-attached or the boot refuses; written freely by the operator's hand and the AI seat on that device; projects to `<projections>/wikis/daemon-<F>/`; refuses every share (`share-face-private`); seeds, exports, imports per face | the REALM WORKBENCH at `realmWorkbenchDocUrl(realm, slug)` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/deterministic-doc.ts`), the realm a private cabal of one the first face founds (`privateCabalRealmId`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/workbench.ts`); written by each face seated `admin`, read by each seated `read`; sealed under the worn owner's content key today (the REST GATE stays OWED, cabal-realm#/the-workbench); ONE mirror folder: the share row's workspace, else `<projections>/wikis/<slug>`, else `<checkout>/wikis/<slug>` beside a sourced canon; seeds once, exports as one row set | `floor-slot/<slug>/working` in the control document, sealed under the vessel's key; a seat that lands LIFTS its rows into the face's workbench, additively |
| ''canon'' | `bags/daemon-<F>` (`daemonFaceCanonBag`): the face's LOCAL canon, minted at its first worn stand, sealed under the face (`standFaceDaemonCanon`); written by the AI's unsigned residency `MOVE` and the hand; projects to `<projections>/bags/daemon-<F>/` | `bags/<slug>`: for a house canon slug the Kahu realm's standing document, written live by the Kahu steward alone (`requireKahuReach`) and read by every other face from the floor's snapshot; for a minted wiki the catalog row's document, written by a holder of its admin cap through an ACTION verb; projects to `bags/<slug>/` where a mirror grant names it | house canon reads from the oracle snapshots; the daemon wiki at the floor reads no canon (`open-daemon-vm.ts`, no face proved) |
| ''libraries'' | `bags/kahua` first (`kahuaRecipe`): the face's lift-only stage, read-only in the composite, moved only by a signed lift or withdraw; projects to `<projections>/bags/kahua-<F>/`; then the vessel's library bags, then `bags/crossroads` (`daemon-vm-core.ts`) | the recipe record's `bag-stack` minus the structural slots, laid at boot and reconciled live (`recipe-watch.ts`) | the floor reads; no private library mirrors (`daemonDiskMirrors` with no face lists crossroads alone, `packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts`) |
| ''own bag'' | `bags/daemon`: the daemon document (bindings), beneath every library, no mirror | none: a domain wiki's own bag stands as its canon | `bags/daemon` |
| ''floor'' | `bags/oracle`, read-only | `bags/oracle`, read-only; a face outside the Kahu cabal reads house canon here | `bags/oracle` |

''What the table says in one breath.'' The daemon wiki keeps every writable layer on one face and one device, and climbs by two crossings (working -> `daemon-<F>` unsigned, `daemon-<F>` -> `kahua-<F>` signed). A domain wiki shares its working layer across a realm's seats, keeps one face's margin in `personal`, and climbs to canon by promotion (`MOVE`) or by an offer the Kahu weighs. The veil floor keeps everything under the vessel's own key until a face lifts it.

''The status door agrees with the mount.'' `wiki_status(recipe="default")` lists the daemon composite's own layers (`composite.layerIds`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts`, `makeWikiStatusReactor`), bottom first: `bags/oracle`, `bags/daemon`, `bags/crossroads`, `bags/kahua`, `bags/daemon-<F>`, `wikis/daemon/working` (the one marked `working`), `wikis/daemon/personal`, `wikis/daemon/draft` and `wikis/daemon/temp`. `personal` and `draft` read mounted writable there, as the table's rows say; `temp` reads unwritable through this door, its `why` reading `bag not registered` (a walked scratch hearth, 2026-11-14). ''OWED'': whether the daemon's `draft` and `personal` device slots project to disk, seed or travel in an export stands unmeasured here.

''The browser vessel.'' The same kernel composes the same stacks (`open-browser-vessel.ts`; the daemon recipe at `open-browser-daemon-vm.ts`, its canon under the same `daemonFaceCanonBag` rule); no disk projector runs there, so no layer of either class projects to a folder from a browser.

!!! Two further classes ~ specified, OWED

No code holds either class today: no bag meta reads a `derived` key, and no door answers `derived-library-read-only`. <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/first-three-wave-map#/the-wikis-in-scope`>> defines both; this slot seats them beside the two that stand.

* ''THE DERIVED LIBRARY'' (road `L40`, `L40b`; OWED). A bag whose records ONE named tool writes as a pure function of ONE named commit of a tracked tree; its first instance, `codemap`, composes into the `lararium` recipe. Its `meta.mem` declares `cap-tier = "public"`, `home = "hearth"` and a new bag-meta key `derived = "<tool>"`, and each record carries the commit it derives from (`head`). It composes only in the ''libraries'' row, beneath the host wiki's canon, under a namespace that canon never writes (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/codemap/`), so it shadows nothing. No hand door writes it: `meme put`, `tiddler put`, a residency `MOVE` or `COPY` naming it, a kāpae and a lift each refuse `derived-library-read-only`. One road writes it, an INGEST wave whose source root the vessel grants to that bag alone (`<LAR_ROOT>/cache/<bag>/<head>/`); a wave replaces the whole bag, and a title the new wave drops retracts to absent (a reveal, #/delete-reveals-or-shadows, since nothing lies beneath its namespace). It never bakes into genesis, never rides a release cut, never takes an offer or a promotion, and never travels in an export or a carry; each of those doors refuses or skips by `derived`. After a re-founding it returns from its cache folder alone, by a fresh ingest. In the layer table it reads as a fourth kind of ''libraries'' row: generator-written, read-only, no mirror.
* ''THE TOPIC WIKI EVERY SEATED FACE WRITES'' (road `L35`; OWED). A domain wiki that one face mints and shares with every face of the operator seated `write`; its first instance, `house`, holds the house's shared memory, and `works` stands beside it as a minted work wiki. Its recipe matches the domain column whole, and it adds a reach law alone: a face reads its own daemon wiki and every topic wiki a share row names it in. Until a workbench's rest seals for its realm's roster (the rest gate, road `C2`), only the owning face writes the workbench on one vessel and every other seated face writes its own `personal`; and until the tiddler door relays to named wikis (road `L17-2a`), its rows ride the steward's daemon wiki at the same titles.

The bag meta law owes the `derived` key beside `cap-tier` and `home` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/delete-reveals-or-shadows`>>

!! Delete ~ reveal or shadow

''Two acts, one gesture word.'' A title can stand in several layers of one recipe at once, and "delete" can mean two different things there:

* ''REVEAL'' (a retract to absent): the topmost record leaves its own layer entirely. The cascade falls through, and whatever a lower layer holds surfaces. Store primitive: `remove` / `removeInBag` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/composite-store.ts`). Disk: no shadow file, and a standing one leaves.
* ''KĀPAE'' (a shadow-tombstone, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae`>> #/core-cut): a tombstone record rises in a writable layer, and every record of the title beneath it stays in its bag yet reads gone. Store primitive: `tombstone` / `tombstoneInBag`; the composite stops at the tombstone (`resolveLayered`, `getLive`). Disk: `<stem>.kapae` where the carrier stood (`packages/lararium-node/src/kapae-shadow.ts`, the projector's `settleShadow`).

Over a title that stands in ONE layer alone, the two acts read the same at the surface and differ beneath: the kāpae stays up and hides any record a lower layer gains later (remove-wins), while the reveal leaves nothing and lets a later arrival show.

!!! The worked case ~ one tiddler in three bags, the user deletes the top

The `elyncia` wiki. Canon `bags/elyncia` holds //Harbor Map// (the table's agreed map); the workbench (`wikis/elyncia/working`) holds the referee's revised map; a player's `personal` layer holds her own annotated copy. She reads her copy, and she presses Delete.

| act | lands | the wiki reads afterward (her face) | the other faces read | a second press |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ''kāpae'' | a tombstone in `personal`, her own layer | //Harbor Map// gone; working and canon keep theirs, shadowed | unchanged: `personal` crosses her devices alone | answers `absent`: nothing stands to delete |
| ''reveal'' | her `personal` record retracts | the referee's revised map, from the workbench | unchanged | reveals canon only where her face writes the workbench (seated `admin`); seated `read` it refuses `reveal-top-unwritable` |

The same press with the title in canon alone (case c) lands the kāpae in the layer a save would take, at or above working, and a reveal refuses, since her face writes no canon. With the title in the workbench and canon (case b), the kāpae lands in the workbench and shadows canon for every seated face; the reveal retracts the workbench record and canon surfaces for every seated face.

!!! What each door does today (measured 2026-11-14)

| door | case (a) top layer only | case (b) top layer and one below | case (c) below only | names the act |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| the TW5 engine's own delete (the hand in the wiki) | kāpae in that layer (`_tombstoneBag`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts`) | kāpae in the top layer, shadowing the lower | kāpae where a save would land: the cascade's layer at or above working, else working | no: always kāpae; a wiki with no working layer refuses by name |
| `meme delete --recipe <slug>` / `meme_delete` | kāpae in that layer | kāpae in the top layer where it stands above the designated bag, else in the designated bag (`deleteThroughRecipe`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts`) | kāpae in the designated bag (`writable-bag`, the working slot) | no: always kāpae; the receipt names `tombstonedIn` and `readFrom` |
| `meme delete` on the anchor (`recipe: "default"`) | kāpae through the daemon wiki's engine (`wikiMemeSink`, `place-meme.ts`), so the adaptor's law above | same | same | no |
| `meme delete --bag <bag>` | kāpae IN the named bag (`removeMeme` over that bag's sink) | kāpae in the named bag; shadows only what lies beneath that bag in a recipe that composes it | kāpae in the named bag | no |
| `lares tiddler delete` / `tiddler_delete` (the anchor alone today) | `mode: "kapae"` (default): tombstone in working; `mode: "reveal"`: retract | kapae: the act names `holds` and `shadowed`; reveal: retract, `reveals` names the lower bag, and a leave reads `revealed-from:<bag>` | kapae: tombstone in working; reveal: refuses `reveal-top-unwritable`, since the layer that holds the record sits beneath working and takes no hand's delete | YES: `mode` (`--mode`), defaulting `kapae`; refuses `delete-mode-unknown` on any other word (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts`) |
| `lares act CLEAR` / `DROP` | kāpae over every live title IN the named bag (`executeClear`, `executeDrop`, `action-handler.ts`) | same | — | no: exclusion gestures, kāpae by law |
| `lares act MOVE` (promotion), an INGEST re-link | the source RETRACTS (reveal): the title lands in the target, then leaves the source | same | — | no: relocation, reveal by law |

''The default every door takes: kāpae.'' Three grounds. (1) The resurrection guard: a user who deletes what she reads expects it gone; a reveal that surfaces a lower copy she never saw replays the OverlayFS resurrection (kapae#/core-cut). (2) Remove-wins under contention: a raised kāpae holds against a peer re-adding a lower copy, and a retract holds against nothing. (3) Every door already raised kāpae before the name stood, so the default changes no landed behaviour. ''A reveal rides by name'' (`mode: "reveal"`), the act of a hand that wants "discard my layer's version; show me what lies beneath".

!!! The tiddler door's delete, as it stands

* ''Which layer takes a delete.'' A layer takes a face's delete only where the island mounts it writable at or above the working layer, and the Kahu predicate and the face's `admin` cap both admit it (`layerFactsFor`). A tombstone shadows only from above, and a canon layer beneath working takes no hand's delete.
* ''What a reveal refuses.'' A reveal retracts the topmost record of the title. Where that record's layer sits beneath working, or the face cannot write it, the reveal refuses `reveal-top-unwritable` and names the layer; a reveal of a record no mounted layer holds (the engine's own, or a wiki with no store beneath it) refuses the same, with nothing to retract. Each refusal names `mode: "kapae"` as the act that would shadow it from working.
* ''A refusal answers a receipt.'' The door answers `decision: "refused"` with `refusal`, `why`, the record's `hash` and the `consequence` it read, and lands nothing; it never throws for a refusal the family law reads. Outside the law the door still throws by name: an unknown mode word (`delete-mode-unknown`), a system title (`tiddler-put-code-class`), and a read the face's cap denies.
* ''What the consequence names.'' Each act row carries `holds` (every layer with a live record of the title) and, by mode, `shadowed` (the layers a kāpae hides) or `reveals` (the layer that surfaces, `null` where none does or a kāpae stands there). The `leaves` rows give each reason in `why`: `revealed-from:<bag>` for a title that a lower live record now answers, `reveal-keeps:<bag>` for a fellow family member whose layer this hand cannot write and which therefore stays as it reads, `stands-beneath:<bag>` for a record that stays in a layer this hand cannot write, beneath the tombstone that shadows it. `versions` names the titles the consequence itself names (the target, each act, each leave, each orphan) and no other, so an answer stays bounded on a wiki of any size.

!!! A family takes one mode, as one change per layer

A meme's root and its component slots leave together (the family law, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts`, `consequence`): one `mode` covers every member, the consequence reads before anything lands, and each layer takes its members as ONE change (`writeFamily`). The tiddler door refuses a root or slot (`tiddler-delete-in-a-family`, with the consequence) unless the call names the family act (`family: true`, `--family`), and refuses a slot its parent calls by `kahea` even with the flag (the parent's text moves through `meme put`). Cross-layer atomicity cannot exist: a family split across two layers lands as ordered writes, one per layer. `meme delete` on the anchor reads the same consequence, lands one change per member through the daemon wiki's engine (`removeMeme`, `wikiMemeSink`), and takes no mode: kāpae alone (OWED, road `L37`).

!!! How each act travels

| road | kāpae | reveal |
|---|---|---|
| sync | a tombstone record in its document, crossing wherever that document crosses: the workbench to its seated faces, `personal` to one face's devices, the daemon working layer nowhere beyond its device slot | a key leaves its document, crossing the same way |
| disk mirror | `<stem>.kapae` replaces the carrier file (`settleShadow`, `disk-projector.ts`) | the carrier file leaves; no shadow; a standing shadow leaves |
| seed (re-founding) | the mirror's `.kapae` raises the kāpae again through INGEST, remove-wins inside one wave (`seed-mirrors.ts`; `action-handler.ts`, the kāpae an export's shadow files name) | nothing to carry: the folder holds no file |
| export / import | the daemon working layer's `.kapae` files carry as `kapae` rows (`commands/carry.ts`); a workbench's import wave raises them (`wiki-working`, the `kapae` tally) | nothing |
| offer toward house canon | carries nothing: the offer reads the face's view and offers live titles alone (`offerSourceOf`, `canon-offer-verbs.ts`) | nothing |
| promote (`MOVE` of one title) | ''the delete crosses into canon'': a tombstoned source lands a tombstone IN the target and retracts its own (the tombstone road, `executeMove`), and refuses where the target holds nothing unless the hand asks `--shadow` | — (MOVE itself reveals its source) |
| promote (`MOVE` of a whole layer) | skips every tombstone: a layer promotion carries no kāpae (`executeLayerMove`) | — |
| the kahua stage | no kāpae: the stage takes no tombstone; a signed `withdraw` retires an item (kahua-memory-stage#/the-lift), and a daemon-working kāpae over a lifted title shadows it on that device alone (the shadow shows its diff) | — |

!!! How a hand reverses each

* ''A reveal'' reverses by a put: the hand writes the record back into its layer (the version it read stands in the consequence's `versions`).
* ''A kāpae'' reverses two ways today, and neither LOWERS it: a put of a live record over the tombstone replaces it (the hand's new record then shadows the lower copy in its turn), or a retract of the tombstone record itself would reveal the lower copy, and no hand door retracts a tombstone yet (OWED below). `lares wiki resolve <title>` reads which layers hold the title and which tombstone hides it (`makeResolveReactor`, `worker-data-verbs.ts`).

!!! User stories

* ''Gaia 2026 ~ kāpae.'' Keoni keeps a team runbook wiki at work: canon holds the approved procedures, the workbench holds the team's edits. A deprecated procedure still sits in canon until the next review. He deletes it in the workbench; every teammate's wiki reads it gone that afternoon, canon keeps it for the reviewer, and a teammate's laptop that comes back online with a stale copy does not resurrect it.
* ''Gaia 2026 ~ reveal.'' Mele drafted a rewrite of a recipe card in her `personal` layer of the family cookbook wiki, then decided Tūtū's original reads better. She deletes with `reveal`: her rewrite leaves, and Tūtū's card from the workbench shows again, untouched.
* ''Elyncia 5492 ~ kāpae.'' At the Crossroads shrine of Harrowgate, a keeper learns that a ley-line rite in the lifted stage carries a corrupted verse. On her own device she sets it aside in the daemon working layer: the shrine's figure stops reciting it to her at once, the fleet's stage keeps the verse for the elders to judge, and her shadow shows its diff until the elders withdraw the item or re-lift it whole.
* ''Elyncia 5492 ~ reveal.'' A Household shrine's young tender scrawled her own blessing over the family's copy of the harvest litany in her `personal` layer. At the festival she wants the household's words back: she reveals, her scrawl leaves, and the litany the household agreed surfaces beneath it.

!!! OWED

* ''A reveal on every door.'' The TW5 engine's delete, `meme delete` (CLI and `meme_delete`) and the in-wiki UI raise kāpae alone; only the tiddler door names `mode`. The meme door owes `mode: "reveal"` with the same consequence (`retractsOf`), and the wiki UI owes a "show what lies beneath" gesture beside Delete.
* ''A lower-kāpae door for the bag cascade.'' kapae#/law asks a deliberate lower with an effect record; no hand door retracts a tombstone today, and the tiddler door's reveal reads a kāpae'd title as `absent` (the family view reads tombstoned titles as standing nowhere).
* ''kapae#/core-cut and #/law name DELETE among the exclusion gestures (MUST raise kāpae).'' The operator's ask names delete's two meanings; the law owes a re-true: DELETE carries a `mode`, kāpae by default, reveal by name, and only CLEAR, DROP and EVICT stay kāpae-only.
* ''Promotion disagrees with itself over a kāpae.'' A titled `MOVE` of a tombstoned source deletes canon's record (lands a tombstone in canon); a layer `MOVE` skips tombstones. One law owes: does promoting a workbench kāpae delete canon? (An operator ruling.)
* ''No road proposes a canon delete from outside the Kahu.'' The offer carries live titles alone, so a face's kāpae over house canon stays in its workbench or margin; a "propose removal" offer stays unbuilt.
* ''Case (a) under kāpae hides a future lower arrival.'' A kāpae over a title no lower layer held still stands up when canon later gains that title, so the face never sees canon's arrival. Whether a delete with nothing beneath should default to reveal stays an operator question.
* ''A shadow goes unnamed where the view lends no layers.'' A consequence names `holds` and `shadowed` only where its view lends `layersOf` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts`); the meme door's receipt names `tombstonedIn` and no shadowed bags (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts`), so case (b) reads there as a plain tombstone.
* ''A face with no writer's seat.'' `meme delete --recipe <slug>` lands in the record's designated bag (the working slot), which such a face mounts read-only; whether the delete refuses or lands in its `personal` layer stands unwitnessed.
* ''A reveal racing a seated writer's edit'' in the workbench (a retract against a concurrent put, under Automerge's merge): unmeasured.
* ''The domain wiki through the tiddler door'' (lane 2): the door answers the anchor alone, so every row above for a domain wiki reads from the island adaptor and the meme door.
* ''Carry of a `personal` layer's kāpae'' through export and import: unmeasured.

